 "headline": {
  "finding": "no single contract achieves AER-grade coverage cheaply on both grids: at full flip coverage, BERTScore+band costs 4 orderings on de-en but 15/102 (15%) on zh-en; AER costs 1/109 and 1/102 (1%) on both grids with one registered CI procedure. On de-en BERTScore covers by abstaining (all 11 flip-pair point deltas ~0), i.e. it cannot order the flipping pairs at all.",
  "equal_budget_note": "r60 singles coverage (9-10/14) already uses the SAME bootstrap tie rule as AER (col_mat per contract, identical indices) - the equal-budget comparison is in the paper; this sweep adds the cheaper fixed-band variant."
 }
